  "finalMessage": "Role: INDEPENDENT REVIEWER (read-only). Files changed: none.\n\nReview of Round 4d (Q240-Q245, S140-S142):\n- (1) Pinned bar: Sits outside scroll area above `imePadding()`, pinned above keyboard; other editors default to `bottomBar = null` and render identically.\n- (2) Panel queue: Advances only on chained draft ID change; survives chained drafts; deduplicates IDs via `resolveLabPanel`; preserves date and labName; clears on chip retap/single test chip click.\n- (3) Flag rule: Pure `labResultFlag()` helper used; no UI regex, parsing, or invented clinical thresholds.\n- (4) Unknown flag: Guarded by `flag != LabResultFlag.UNKNOWN`; manual doctor switch selection is never overwritten when result is unparsable or text.\n- (5) Custom tests: `bothEmpty` immediately reveals `labUnit` and `labRefRange` fields; \"Edit unit and range\" unlocks existing ones.\n- (6) Test tags: All S142 testTags preserved; no visible \"Codex\" wording.\n- (7) A11y & theme: 48 dp `minimumTouchTarget()`, theme colors, weighted 1-row buttons with `softWrap = false`.\n- (8) Scope: No dead code or unauthorized file edits.\n\nFindings:\n- Should-fix: `PatientEditor.kt:509` `Box(modifier = Modifier.fillMaxWidth().verticalScroll(rememberScrollState()).padding(...))` — redundant `verticalScroll` on pinned bar container may intercept vertical touch gestures.\n- Nit: `LabEditor.kt:201, 211, 221` `Text(..., maxLines = 1, softWrap = false)` — consider adding `overflow = TextOverflow.Ellipsis` for extreme font scaling.\n\nVerification:\n- `python3 .agents/checks/check_r4d.py`: PASS (S140, S141, S142).\n- Unit tests (`LabResultFlagTest`, `LabPanelResolveTest`): not run (Gradle daemon IPC blocked by sandbox).",
